,\n            \"These annotations are based on computational predictions. The programs that generate these annotations look for patterns in the protein's sequence (like specific domains or targeting signals) that are similar to other, well-studied proteins known to be located in the vacuole.\\n\",\n            \"\\n\",\n            \"The key part is the **\\\"IEA\\\"** tag at the end of each term. This is an evidence code that stands for **\\\"Inferred from Electronic Annotation.\\\"** It means the \\\"vacuolar\\\" location was assigned automatically by a computer program, not by a human curator looking at experimental results.\\n\",\n            \"\\n\",\n            \"**In summary:** The protein is called **\\\"hypothetical\\\"** because its function has not been experimentally confirmed, and it is classified as **\\\"vacuolar\\\"** because computational models predict it has features that would send it to the vacuole. Both labels reflect that our knowledge about this protein is based on prediction, not direct laboratory proof.\\n\",\n            \"------------------------------\\n\",\n            \"\\n\",\n            \"🧬 GFF Query: quit\\n\",\n            \"👋 Goodbye!\\n\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n      \"source\": [],\n      \"metadata\": {\n        \"id\": \"GduKaqYo6W8y\"\n      },\n      \"execution_count\": null,\n      \"outputs\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n      \"metadata\": {\n        \"id\": \"dSZzrj4dRQDo\"\n      },\n      \"source\": [\n        \"#**Cloud models of OpenAi**\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n      \"execution_count\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {\n        \"id\": \"DPc57ofQpRxc\",\n        \"colab\": {\n          \"base_uri\": \"https://localhost:8080/\"\n        },\n        \"outputId\": \"e93a3b21-e822-4dfd-ae1d-34aec7f2e8de\",\n        \"collapsed\": true\n      },\n      \"outputs\": [\n        {\n          \"output_type